          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            %strong Differential (pre-)graded vector spaces.
            (We continue from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector spaces
            with the terminology of pre-gvs for the general case and gvs for the positively or negatively graded ones.)
          %p
            A
            = succeed "," do
              %strong differential (pre-)graded vector space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is a (pre-)graded vector space and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \in Hom_{-1}(V,V)
            satisfies
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial\circ\partial = 0
          %p
            This endomorphism,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            or sometimes the
            %em boundary operator
            of the dgvs.
          %p
            To link it with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+object"} differential object
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+translation"} category with translation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial : V\to s(V)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            of vector spaces. (Some questions of terminology are addressed further down this entry.)
          %p
            As usual,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ker
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Im
                  %mo ∂
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ker \partial / Im \partial
            is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(V,\partial)
          %p
            Let
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V',\partial')
            be two pre-dgvs
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℤ
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(V,V') = \bigoplus_{p\in \mathbb{Z}}Hom_p(V,V')
          %p is a pre-dgvs with differential
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Df
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi f
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo ∂
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Df = \partial'\circ f - (-1)^{|f|}f\circ\partial
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            homogeneous.
          %p
            A degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            linear morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is
            %em compatible with the differentials
            if it is a cycle for this differential
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Df
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Df = 0
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi r
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial' f = (-1)^{r}f\partial.
          %p
            A
            %strong morphism between pre-dgvs
            is a linear morphism of degree 0 that is compatible with the differentials:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: (V,\partial)\to (V',\partial').
          %p
            This induces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(f): H(V,\partial)\to H(V',\partial').
          %p
            We get a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi pre
                  %mo −
                  %mi DGVS
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pre -  DGVS
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is a functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo :
                    %mi pre
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mi DGVS
                    %mo →
                    %mi pre
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mi GVS
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H : pre\! -\! DGVS\to pre\!-\! GVS
          %h3#weak_equivalences Weak equivalences
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: (V,\partial)\to (V',\partial')
            in {\sf pre-DGVS}, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a
            %strong weak equivalence
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(f)
            is an isomorphism. In this case we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: (V,\partial)\stackrel{\simeq}{\to} (V',\partial')
          %h3#homotopies Homotopies
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,f' : (V,\partial)\to (V',\partial')
            be two morphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi pre
                    %mo −
                    %mi DGVS
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pre-DGVS
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
            are
            %strong homotopic
            denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∼
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\sim f'
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo −
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f-f'
            is a boundary in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Hom(V,V'),D)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h : V \to V'
            of degree +1 such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo −
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mi Dh
                    %mo =
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo ′
                    %mi h
                    %mo +
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f-f' = Dh = \partial' h + h\partial
          %p
            %strong Contractible and Acyclic DGVSs
          %p
            A dgvs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)
            is
            %em contractible
            if the identity map on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is homotopic to the zero morphism and is
            %em acyclic
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(V,\partial) = 0
          %p
            %strong Remarks
          %p
            (i) A
            %em contracting homotopy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi V
                  %mo ∼
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h : Id_V \sim O_V
            is a degree 1 map such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial h(x) + h(\partial x) = x
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_p
          %p
            (ii) If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)
            is contractible, then it is acyclic and conversely. The converse depends strongly on our working with vector spaces. If we worked with modules over a commutative ring,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)
            is acyclic and projective in each dimension, then it is contractible.’‘ This is important when looking at, for instance, diagrams of dgvs since even if each individual object in the diagram may be contractible, it might be impossible to pick the contracting homotopies to give a map of diagrams, i.e., to be compatible with the structural maps.
          %h3#suspension_for_pre_dgvs Suspension for (pre-) dgvs
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)
            is a pre-dgvs, then its
            = succeed "-suspension" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mi rV
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s^rV,\partial)
            = succeed "-suspension," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mi rV
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^rV
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            together with the differential
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mi rv
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi rs
                  %msup
                    %mo
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial s^rv = (-1)^rs^r(\partial v).
          %h3#tensor_product_of_pre_dgvs Tensor product of (pre-) dgvs
          %p
            If
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V',\partial')
            are pre-dgvs, then we give the tensor product,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\otimes V'
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi v
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi v
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi v
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mi v
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial(v\otimes v') = (\partial v) \otimes v' + (-1)^{|v|}v \otimes (\partial' v' ),
          %p
            and we denote the result by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)\otimes (V', \partial')
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kunneth+theorem"} Kunneth theorem
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H((V,\partial)\otimes (V', \partial')) \cong H(V,\partial)\otimes H(V', \partial').
          %h3#duals_of_predgvs Duals of (pre-)dgvs
          %p
            The dual
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo #
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo #
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo #
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#(V,\partial) = (\# V,\#\partial)
            of a pre-dgvs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)
            is given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo #
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \# V
            with differential
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo #
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi t
                    %mo ∂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\# \partial ) = - ^t \partial
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo #
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi f
                  %mo ;
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi f
                  %mo ;
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle(\# \partial)f; v\rangle + (-1)^{|f|}\langle f; \partial v\rangle = 0.
          %h3#chains_and_cochains_terminology Chains and cochains: terminology
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)
            is a pre-dgvs with ‘lower grading’ that is the summands are written
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)
            may be called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            and terms such as
            = succeed "," do
              %em cycle
            = succeed "," do
              %em boundary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            are used with the usual meanings.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\partial)
            is presented with the ‘upper grading’, so
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^p
          %p There is no real distinction between the two cases in the abstract, but in applications there is often a fixed ‘dimensional’ interpretation and then the ‘natural’ and ‘geometric’ aspects determine which is more appropriate or useful.
